  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n        ««  Shadow Hearts  »»                                   [A-1-05]\n____________________________________________________________________________\n\\\\\\\\¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\\\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\                                Items                                \\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\_____________________________________________________________________\\\\\\\\\n   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\nListed here are all of the Items in the game, in the order that the game lists\nthem.\n\n\n.—————————————————————.———————————————————————————————————————————————————.———.\n|  Item               |  Effect           Usable in the Command Menu? ——> | Y |\n'—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Description (Info)                                                         |\n|                                                                             |\n'—————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————'\n\n\n.—————————————————————.———————————————————————————————————————————————————.———.\n|  Thera Leaf         |  Restores 75 HP                                   | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Thera Leaf                                                                 |\n|  Long used for its medicinal properties, this herb blooms only once each    |\n|  year. Those lucky enough to see the small blossom are said to enjoy good   |\n|  health for the year.                                                       |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Thera Seed         |  Restores 150 HP                                  | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Thera Seed                                                                 |\n|  The seeds of the medicinal herb Thera Leaf. Extremely nourishing, they     |\n|  greatly restore physical strength when ingested. No taste. Easily          |\n|  portable, they are valued highly by adventurers.                           |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Thera Root         |  Restores 300 HP                                  | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Thera Root                                                                 |\n|  Gathered from the Thera Leaf plant 5 years after the blossoms appear.      |\n|  Each plant has only one precious root. It dramatically restores physical   |\n|  strength.                                                                  |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Thera Extract      |  Fully restores HP                                | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Thera Extract                                                              |\n|  Extract of the Thera Root further refined and purified. It has excellent   |\n|  restorative properties for physical strength. Difficult to make and very   |\n|  scarce.                                                                    |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Mana Leaf          |  Restores 50 MP                                   | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Mana Leaf                                                                  |\n|  A mystical, scarlet herb that grows in secret places. When taken by those  |\n|  with psychic or magic abilities, consumed mystical strength is again       |\n|  restored.                                                                  |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Mana Seed          |  Restores 100 MP                                  | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Mana Seed                                                                  |\n|  The seed of the mystical herb Mana Leaf, born only once every 2 years and  |\n|  having a hard shell. Dried under moonlight. Restores lost mystical         |\n|  strength.                                                                  |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Mana Root          |  Restores 200 MP                                  | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Mana Root                                                                  |\n|  Main root of the mystical herb Mana Leaf. Taken from the mature plant and  |\n|  exposed to the light of 20 full-moon nights. Powerful restorer of          |\n|  mystical strength.                                                         |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Mana Extract       |  Fully restores MP                                | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Mana Extract                                                               |\n|  A secret medicine made by putting the extract of Mana Roots under a        |\n|  magical process. Gives off a perfume and a blue glow. It fully restores    |\n|  mystical strength.                                                         |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Pure Leaf          |  Restores 3 SP                                    |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Pure Leaf                                                                  |\n|  A magical herb used by ancient magic users such as shamans when            |\n|  practicing their craft. It changes the secretions of the brain,            |\n|  influencing one's state of mind.                                           |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Pure Seed          |  Restores 6 SP                                    |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Pure Seed                                                                  |\n|  The seeds of the magical Pure Leaf, soaked in a special medicinal liquid   |\n|  for 15 years. They have a powerful tranquilizing effect.                   |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Pure Root          |  Restores 10 SP                                   |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Pure Root                                                                  |\n|  The root of the magical Pure Leaf. Made from the most poisonous part, but  |\n|  made safe to ingest. Makes one fearless of death or the enemy in battle.   |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Pure Extract       |  Fully restores SP                                |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Pure Extract                                                               |\n|  Concentrated, distilled liquid of Pure Root. It contains fragments of      |\n|  spirit stone. When ingested, one feels a great sense of exhilaration.      |\n|  Warriors have long used it before taking on mighty enemies.                |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  TalismanOfLuck     |  Restores Unconscious person's HP 30%             |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  TalismanOfLuck                                                             |\n|  A cloth talisman embroidered in silk with pictures describing the Laws of  |\n|  Space. It can return the bearer from Unconsciousness and restore a small   |\n|  amount of strength.                                                        |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  TalismanOfMercy    |  Restores Unconscious person's HP 50%             |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Talisman of Mercy                                                          |\n|  A papyrus talisman with a picture of the holy man Hylas on it. Infused     |\n|  with the fragrance of incense, it awakens the Unconscious traveler and     |\n|  restores his strength.                                                     |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  TalismanOfWisdom   |  Restores Unconscious person's HP 30% and         |   |\n|                     |  restores 50 MP.                                  |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Talisman of Wisdom                                                         |\n|  A talisman bearing a portrait of the theologian and philosopher Somel.     |\n|  Awakens one from Unconsciousness and restores physical and mystical        |\n|  strength.                                                                  |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  TalismanOfPurity   |  Restores Unconscious person's HP 30% and         |   |\n|                     |  restores 3 SP.                                   |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Talisman of Purity                                                         |\n|  Goatskin talisman cured in holy water. Upon it, painted in mineral dyes,   |\n|  is a crudely beautiful painting of the sky through a window. Returns       |\n|  bearer from Unconsciousness and restores physical and mental strength.     |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  TalismanOfPower    |  Fully restores Unconscious person's HP, MP,      |   |\n|                     |  and SP                                           |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Talisman of Power                                                          |\n|  A talisman bearing the buried shrine crest, made from some unknown         |\n|  material. Fully restores physical, mystical and mental strength and cures  |\n|  Unconsciousness.                                                           |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Mermaid's Tear     |  Cures Poison                                     |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Mermaid's Tear                                                             |\n|  The number of facets on this gem represent a holy number. This deep blue   |\n|  gem is cut from an ore excavated from undersea ruins. With its mysterious  |\n|  detoxifying properties, it is very useful to adventurers traveling         |\n|  unexplored regions.                                                        |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Holy Mother Bust   |  Cures Confusion                                  |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Holy Mother Bust                                                           |\n|  A small statue of the head of a woman, it cures Confusion. It is modeled   |\n|  after the figure of his mother a martyred sculptor carved into the stone   |\n|  of his prison.                                                             |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Angel's Feather    |  Cures Paralysis                                  |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Angel's Feather                                                            |\n|  A Shinto artifact made from light blue metal that has undergone a          |\n|  mystical process, it cures Paralysis. Although it is metal, it is          |\n|  extremely flexible and light, hence the name \"Angel's Feather\".            |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Faerie's Sigh      |  Cures Silence                                    |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Faerie's Sigh                                                              |\n|  A small relief carving of a girl with wings, it cures Silence. In the      |\n|  Middle Ages, reproductions were all the rage among noblewomen.             |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Imp's Fang         |  Cures Petrification                              |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Imp's Fang                                                                 |\n|  Thought to be a fossil from some mysterious ancient creature. Effective    |\n|  in curing Petrification, some mountain tribes even now wear it as a charm  |\n|  from infancy.                                                              |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Phoenix Tail       |  Cancels out all Judgment Ring abnormalities      |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Phoenix Tail                                                               |\n|  A tail feather from the sacred phantom bird. When used, it emits a blue    |\n|  flame and cancels out all effects on the Judgment Ring.                    |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Soul Benediction   |  Cures all Status abnormalities                   |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Soul Benediction                                                           |\n|  A rare woodblock engraved with an image of the mythic nymph Daphne. Cures  |\n|  all Status abnormalities--Poison, Paralysis, Petrification, Confusion and  |\n|  Silence.                                                                   |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  TeaOfTheHealer     |  Restores 75 HP and 50 MP                         | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Tea of the Healer                                                          |\n|  Tea prepared in the manner originated by the healer Shuju. Brewed from     |\n|  sacred leaves, it restores physical and mystical strength when imbibed     |\n|  with a pure heart.                                                         |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  TeaOfTheSage       |  Restores 150 HP and 100 MP                       | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  TeaOfTheSage                                                               |\n|  A secret medicine passed down through the generations of the conquering    |\n|  Sou family, it dramatically restores the physical and mystical strength    |\n|  of soldiers.                                                               |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  TeaOfTheHolyOne    |  Restores 300 HP and 200 MP                       | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Tea of the Holy One                                                        |\n|  The secret medicine prepared by Saint Ignatius. Restores physical and      |\n|  mystical strength. It gives off a red glow under the light of the moon.    |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Fruit of Yggdrasil |  Fully restores HP and MP                         | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Fruit of Yggdrasil                                                         |\n|  Musky fruit of the mystical tree whose top reaches up into the heaves and  |\n|  whose roots descend into Hell. It restores physical and mystical strength  |\n|  completely.                                                                |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Witch's Broth      |  Restores 50 MP and 3 SP                          | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Witch's Broth                                                              |\n|  A brew of secret black magic ingredients. Every mouthful brings an ever-   |\n|  changing series of flavors. It restores mystical and mental strength.      |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Priest's Wine      |  Restores 100 MP and 6 SP                         | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Priest's Wine                                                              |\n|  Wine made by the miracle-worker priest Rasfarus by adding his own and a    |\n|  few drops of a woman's blood to muddy water. Restores mystical and mental  |\n|  strength.                                                                  |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Alchemist'sWater   |  Restores 200 MP and 10 SP                        | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Alchemist's Water                                                          |\n|  Distilled water the alchemist Gala, who lives to be 400 years old,         |\n|  accidentally discovered trying to produce platinum. Restores mystical and  |\n|  mental strength.                                                           |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Eye of Ouroboros   |  Fully restores MP and SP                         | Y |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Eye of Ouroboros                                                           |\n|  A religious artifact of elaborate workmanship, studded with gem beads.     |\n|  Many crude replicas exist, but the original fully restores mystical and    |\n|  mental strength.                                                           |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Bronze Arrowhead   |  User's hit area doubles                          |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Bronze Arrowhead                                                           |\n|  Long used for hunting by mountain tribes with mystic powers. It doubles    |\n|  the width of the Judgment Ring hit area, although only for the user.       |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Bronze Dagger      |  All allies' hit areas double                     |   ||—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Bronze Dagger                                                              |\n|  A mystical hunting tool with the same origins as the Bronze Arrowhead.     |\n|  When used, it doubles the width of the Judgment Ring hit areas for all     |\n|  allies.                                                                    |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Silver Hourglass   |  User's indicator sweeps half as fast             |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Silver Hourglass                                                           |\n|  An hourglass filled with granules of silver. Slows the speed of the        |\n|  indicator's sweep around the Judgment Ring by half, but only for the       |\n|  user.                                                                      |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  Gold Hourglass     |  All allies' indicators sweep half as fast        |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Gold Hourglass                                                             |\n|  An hourglass filled with granules of gold. Slows the speed of the          |\n|  indicator's sweep around the Judgment Ring by half for all allies.         |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  W.Tiger Hair       |  User's hit area is cut in half, but Attack       |   |\n|                     |  Power doubles.                                   |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Hair of White Tiger                                                        |\n|  A spiritual artifact shaped like the beard of the White Tiger, a god of    |\n|  the four directions. User's Attack Power is doubled, but hit area is cut   |\n|  in half.                                                                   |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  B.Dragon Horn      |  All allies' hit areas are cut in half, but       |   |\n|                     |  Attack Powers double                             |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Horn of Blue Dragon                                                        |\n|  A spiritual artifact shaped like the horn of the Blue Dragon, a god of     |\n|  the four directions. Allies' Attack Powers are doubled, but hit areas are  |\n|  cut in half.                                                               |\n|_____________________________________________________________________________|\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|¯¯¯|\n|  B.Tortoise Fang    |  User's indicator sweeps twice as fast, but       |   |\n|                     |  Attack Power doubles.                            |   |\n|—————————————————————'———————————————————————————————————————————————————'———|\n|  Fang of Black Tortoise                                                     |\n|  A spiritual artifact shaped l